@startuml sequence_diagram
autonumber

title Flower Shop -- Sequence Diagram: Admin Adds a Flower Through API Client

actor Admin
participant WebClient
participant ApiController
participant FlowerService
participant AddFlowerCommand
participant FlowerRepository
participant NotificationService

== 1. Login ==

Admin -> WebClient : enter credentials
WebClient -> ApiController : POST /api/login {email, password}
ApiController --> WebClient : {user}
WebClient --> Admin : show admin controls

== 2. Submit New Flower ==

Admin -> WebClient : submit flower form
WebClient -> ApiController : POST /api/flowers {name, color, price, stock}
ApiController -> FlowerService : add_new_flower(...)
FlowerService -> AddFlowerCommand : execute()
AddFlowerCommand -> FlowerRepository : add_flower(...)
FlowerRepository --> AddFlowerCommand : saved
AddFlowerCommand --> FlowerService : done

== 3. Send Notification ==

FlowerService -> NotificationService : notify("CREATED", flower, email)
NotificationService --> FlowerService : ok
FlowerService --> ApiController : created id
ApiController --> WebClient : 201 {flower}

== 4. Refresh Catalog ==

WebClient -> ApiController : GET /api/flowers
ApiController -> FlowerRepository : get_filtered_sorted()
FlowerRepository --> ApiController : [flowers list]
ApiController --> WebClient : {flowers}
WebClient --> Admin : render updated catalog

@enduml
